<title>CANADA: Golden Rule, Hixon shares continue rise.</title>
<headline>Golden Rule, Hixon shares continue rise.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in junior gold exploration firms Golden Rule Resources Ltd and Hixon Gold Resources Inc continued to climb on Thursday, buoyed by preliminary results from Hixon's Stenpad property in Ghana.</p>
<p>&quot;They released trenching samples a couple of days ago and they are great,&quot; said one trader.</p>
<p>&quot;Besides, the minute you get a whiff of a gold play, the money move (into the stocks) is phenomenal,&quot; he added.</p>
<p>Golden Rule rose 1.05 to 7.70, off a high of 7.85, in brisk trade on the Toronto Stock Exchange while Hixon was up 0.40 at 7.60 on the Vancouver Stock Exchange.</p>
<p>((Reuters Toronto Bureau (416) 941-8100))</p>
</text>
